    narr:narration """The application of the signed-manifest gate is currently framed through a series of [formal, authority-driven decisions](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_1) that prioritize conservation and system stability. These [technical, present-tense mandates](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_3) establish a consistent, legitimate baseline for deployment environments, focusing on the structural requirements of the gate. While the prevailing discourse emphasizes [abstract technical compliance](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_4), there is a distinct shift toward [self-enhancement](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5) when evaluating the gate's performance in concrete, real-time scenarios. The narrative trajectory is currently anchored in these authoritative, decision-oriented probes, which collectively define the gate as a necessary, non-negotiable component of the deployment lifecycle.""" ;
